# ROAST writes its outputs next to the subject MRI. A single run of the
# MNI152 example is ~650 MB, and three of its files exceed GitHub's 100 MB
# limit, so none of it belongs in the repository - it is all reproducible
# from the tracked inputs.

# ROAST derives a lot of filenames from the subject's: _ras, _T1orT2_,
# _T1andT2_, _1mm, _padded<N>, _MNI, the c1..c6 tissue maps, _seg8, _rmask,
# and a <subject>_YYYYMMDDThhmmss tag per run. Enumerating those suffixes
# proved to be whack-a-mole, so ignore the whole directory and list the
# tracked inputs instead - they are a fixed, known set.
#
# Adding a new subject MRI here therefore needs an explicit `git add -f`.
example/*
!example/MNI152_T1_1mm.nii
!example/subject1.nii
!example/subject1_T2.nii
!example/subject1_customLocations
!example/nyhead_T1orT2_SPM_masks.nii.zip
!example/nyhead_T1orT2_seg8.mat

# 3. Error log written by runExamples.m and examples/run_examples.py
errLog.txt

# Octave MEX built from SPM12 source (see octave-compat/README.md)
lib/spm12/**/*.mex
lib/spm12/src/

# Example-suite scaffolding (see octave-compat/scripts/)
roast-suite-work/
master_cmds.json

# Python caches
__pycache__/
*.pyc
